[00:17.00]predecessor n. 前任；祖先 示例 ① In 1964, Knight and Bowerman contributed $500 each to form Blue Ribbon Sports, the predecessor of Nike. 1964年，奈特和鲍尔曼各出资500美元成立了蓝带运动品公司，这就是耐克公司的前身。（2008. 12） ② The new president kept many of the policies of his predecessor. 新总统保留了许多前任总统的政策。
[00:24.83]aggressive a. 好斗的，富于攻击性的，侵略的 示例 ① The school aggressively pushed mentoring of minorities by other students and "partnering" with parents at a special pre-enrollment session. 该校大力推行其他学生对少数民族学生的辅导，以及在入学前这一特殊时期与家长的“合作”。（2011. 6） ② They launched an aggressive advertising campaign. 他们发起了声势浩大的广告宣传活动。
[00:32.19]according to prep. 据…所说；按照… 示例 ① According to data gathered by Harvard Law School professor Lani Guinier, the most selective schools are more likely to choose blacks who have at least one immigrant parent from Africa or the Caribbean than black students who are descendants of American slaves. 根据哈佛大学法学院教授拉尼•吉尼尔收集的数据，录取条件最苛刻的大学更倾向于招收那些父母中至少有一方是非洲或加勒比海地区移民的黑人学生，而不愿招收那些美国奴隶的后代。（2011. 6） ② According to the report, this girl was murdered. 据报道，这个女孩是被谋杀的。
[00:40.16]literally ad. 字面上，照字面意义地 示例 ① China has to find a way to continue its rapid growth without choking to death. Literally. 中国得找到一条能保持快速增长且又不会让人窒息而死（注：暗指空气污染）的发展之路。一点儿没错。（www.realclearpolitics.com）② You cannot understand my word just literally. 你不能仅仅从字面上来理解我说的话。
[00:46.59]campus n. （大学、学院的）校园，校区 示例 ① For years private colleges such as Princeton and MIT have had success bringing minorities onto campus in the summer before freshman year to give them some preparatory courses. 多年来， 诸如普林斯顿和麻省理工之类的私立大学已经成功让少数民族学生在新生报到前的夏季来校上一些预科课程。（2011. 6） ② I take a walk on the campus every morning. 我每天清晨在校园里散步。
[00:53.02]vicinity n.周围地区，附近 示例 ① Then you enter your street name or postcode and it will tell you all the bus stops in the vicinity—and how long you will have to wait for a bus; not just the first bus, but a series of buses. 然后你输入你所在的街名或者邮政编码，网站将告诉你在你附近的全部公交站，并告诉你你需要等多久；不只是第一班车，而是一系列的班车。（The Daily Telegraph）② There is no supermarket in the vicinity of our house. 我家附近没有超市。
[01:00.66]machinery n. 机器，大型机器；机械装置 示例 ① Investment spending on machinery, buildings and infrastructure accounted for over half of China's growth last year. 去年，在机械、建筑和基础设施方面的投资占中国总增长的一半以上。（The Economist） ② We should found the machinery for resolving disputes. 我们应该创建一个解决纠纷的机构。
[01:06.23]current a. 流行的；当前的，现在的‖n. (水、 电、气)流；潮流 示例 ① That's because the quest for a unified theory that would account for all the forces of nature has pushed current mathematics to its limits. 那是因为大家都在探索能够解释大自然各种力量的一统理论，而这种努力已把当代数学推向极限。（2010. 12）② How about your current employer? 你现在的雇主怎么样？
[01:12.08]cable n. 缆绳；电缆；电报‖v. 发电报 示例 ① Part of the problem is that with wall to wall Internet and cable news, every missing child case gets so much airtime that it's not surprising even normal parental anxiety can be amplified. 部分原因是在网络和电视铺天盖地的新闻报道中， 每个儿童失踪案件的报道时间如此之长，以至于父母的正常焦虑情绪可能被放大也就不足为奇了。（2009. 6） ② Here, we can receive almost 50 cable channels. 在这儿，我们能接收到近50个有线电视频道。
[01:19.38]lawn n. 草坪，草地 示例 ① "Who's going to mow the lawn?" I asked my husband this morning. 今天早晨，我问我的丈夫：“谁来修剪草坪？”（2011. 6） ② Workers have to mow the lawn once a week in summer. 夏天， 工人们每周都要修剪一次草坪。
[01:25.23]formal a. 正规的；正式的；形式上的 示例 ① I'd rather not make it something formal and structured. 我希望不要把（料理花园）这件事搞得那么正式和格式化。（2012. 12）② These children did not receive formal education. 这些孩子没有受过正规教育。
[01:33.77]hamper v. 妨碍，阻止 示例 ① Widespread academic fraud may hamper a drive for innovation. 学术造假泛滥或许会遏制创新的动力。（The Economist）② The lack of modern technology has hampered agricultural production. 先进机械的缺乏阻碍了农业生产。
[01:40.67]widespread a. 广泛的，普遍的 示例 ① Technology advances, including the widespread availability of broadband, are making the introduction of remote working a piece of cake. 包括宽带普及在内的技术进步使远程办公变得非常容易。（2009. 12）② The rumours and slanders about this girl are widespread. 到处散播着关于这个女孩的流言飞语。
[01:47.38]crucial a. 关键性的，至关重要的 示例 ① One crucial aspect of Einstein's training that is overlooked is the years of philosophy he read as a teenager—Kant, Schopenhauer and Spinoza, among others. 人们都忽视了一点，爱因斯坦在青少年时期阅读了大量哲学书籍，囊括了康德、 叔本华、斯宾诺莎以及其他一些哲学家的思想，这是他所接受的教育当中至关重要的一部分。（2010. 12） ② Parents play a crucial role in their children's education. 父母对孩子的教育起到至关重要的作用。
[01:54.01]define v. 下定义；明确；画出…的线条 示例 ① The Affluent Society is a modern classic because it helped define a new moment in the human condition. 《富裕社会》是一本现代经典著作，因为它有助于定义一种崭新的人类生存状况。（2007. 6） ② It is difficult to define the meaning of this word. 这个词很难定义。
[02:01.75]inherit v. 继承；接任；经遗传获得某种品质、 特征等 示例 ① What are you going to do with the old house you've inherited from your grandfather? 你打算怎样处置从你祖父那里继承的旧房子？（2010. 12）② This is an inherited disease which is difficult to treat. 这是一种很难治疗的遗传病。
[02:08.13]distinguish v. 区分；使有别于；认出；使著名 示例 ① Sydney Brenner, senior distinguished fellow of the Crick-Jacobs Center in California, won the 2002 Nobel Prize for Medicine and says that if there is a global disaster some humans will survive—and evolution will favour small people with bodies large enough to support the required amount of brain power. 加利福尼亚克里克雅各布中心的著名高级研究员悉尼•布伦纳 2002年获得了诺贝尔医学奖，他说如果发生全球性灾难的话， 一些人将能生存下来，进化将偏爱身形瘦小却足以支持所需脑力的人们。（2008. 6） ② It is hard for children to distinguish between right and wrong. 让小孩懂得区分对与错是很难的。
[02:16.74]stimulate v. 激发；刺激；促进（身体某部分的） 功能 示例 ① It may stimulate scientists to make further studies. 这可能会刺激科学家作进一步的研究。（2012. 12）② The report can be used to stimulate discussion among the students. 这篇报道可以用来激发学生们的讨论。
[02:24.13]tackle v. 应付，解决 示例 ① McDonald's, Greggs, KFC and Subway are today named as the most littered brands in England as Keep Britain Tidy called on fast-food companies to do more to tackle customers who drop their wrappers and drinks cartons in the streets. 如今，麦当劳、格雷格斯、肯德基和赛百味被“保持英国清洁行动”称为英国最垃圾的品牌。该行动号召快餐公司付出更多努力，解决那些顾客在大街上乱丢包装和饮料盒的行为。（2009. 12） ② The government is prepared to tackle the refugee issue. 政府准备解决难民问题。
[02:31.07]deficit n. 赤字，亏损；缺款额，缺少 示例 ① The larger the trade deficit, the smaller the GDP. 贸易逆差越大，国内生产总值越小。（2011. 12） ② There is a deficit of $ 2 million to finish the project. 要完成这项工程还缺200万美元。
[02:38.39]summon v. 传唤；召唤；召集；呼吁 示例 ① It was used to summon mobs to particular venues during the riot. 在骚乱过程中，它被用来召唤骚乱者到某个地点集合。（The Economist）② During his holiday, he was urgently summoned to China. 在休假时，他被紧急召去中国。
[02:45.69]elapse v.（时间）流逝 示例 ① Research shows that for protection of your teeth at least 30 minutes should elapse before toothbrushing after an erosive attack. 研究表明，牙齿遭受腐蚀性侵袭后（注：牙釉质变得脆弱），至少要过30分钟才能刷牙， 这样才会起到保护牙齿的作用。（The Washington Post） ② Many years had elapsed before they returned to their mother school. 他们再次回到母校时已经过去很多年了。
[02:53.41]authentic a. 真正的，真迹的；真实的；逼真的 示例 ① Richard Miller, a professor at the University of Michigan, thinks scientists could develop "authentic anti-ageing drugs" by working out how cells in larger animals such as whales and humans resist many forms of injuries. 密歇根大学教授理查德•米勒认为，科学家能够弄明白鲸鱼和人类这样的大型动物体内的细胞如何抵制各种形式伤害的问题，从而开发出“真正的抗衰老药物”。（2008. 6）② They gave us authentic news report. 他们给我们提供了真实的新闻报道。
[02:59.99]pension n. 养老金；退休金；抚恤金 示例 ① Governments in rich countries now accept that their pension and health-care promises will soon become unaffordable, and many of them have embarked on reforms, but so far only timidly. 发达国家的政府已经承认它们很快就会无法履行他们退休金和医疗保障承诺，许多国家也开始着手改革，但迄今为止都是畏首畏尾的改革。（2010. 12） ② This old man lives on a pension. 这个老人靠退休金生活。
[03:06.01]vengeance n. 报仇，复仇，报复 示例 ① A 2008 study by two Harvard economists notes that the "labor-market premium to skill"—or the amount college graduates earned that's greater than what high-school graduate earned—decreased for much of the 20th century, but has come back with a vengeance since the 1980s. 两位哈佛大学经济学家2008年所做的研究指出“劳动力市场付给技术的溢价”—— 即大学毕业生毕业后的收入比高中毕业生收入多出的数量——在20世纪的绝大部分时间里都是下降的，但从20世纪80年代以来却出现了猛烈反弹。（2009. 6）② He swore vengeance on his father's killer. 他发誓要找杀害他父亲的凶手报仇。
[03:12.65]cater v. （为社交活动）提供饮食，承办酒席 示例 ① The service industry, by definition, exists to cater to others' needs. 服务行业顾名思义是为满足他人的需求而存在。（2007. 12） ② This kind of books cater for children. 这种书适合儿童看。
[03:17.11]feeble a. 虚弱的，衰弱的；无效的，缺乏决心的 示例 ① The foreign service is ridiculously feeble—India's 1.2 billion people are represented by about the same number of diplomats as Singapore's 5m. （印度）外事服务部门更是小得可怜，作为一个拥有12 亿人口的大国，其外交人员的数量竟然和只有500万人口的新加坡差不多。（The Economist） ② He told a feeble joke to cheer us up. 为了让我们高兴起来，他讲了一个很无趣的笑话。
[03:23.82]alienate v. 使不友好，离间；使疏远，使格格不入 示例 ① Even small favors can alienate other coworkers and create a hostile environment.甚至一个很小的优惠都会使你与其他同事疏远并创造一个敌对环境。（The Economist） ② This black boy feels alienate from the other white students. 这个黑人男孩觉得与其他白人学生格格不入。
[03:32.87]pledge n. 保证，诺言；抵押‖v. 使保证；正式承诺；抵押 示例 ① A supporter of Awami League leader Sheikh Hasina tries to look at her through a wall of hands raised to pledge support for the party at a rally addressed by Hasina. 在人民联盟领袖谢赫•哈西娜的动员演讲上，一名支持者试图透过那些高高举起宣誓支持该党的“手臂墙”来看看领袖的模样。（The Guardian）② They were all pledged to be loyal to the king. 他们都发誓会对国王忠诚。
[03:40.89]economy n. 经济；经济制度；节约 示例 ① One great challenge for the U.S. economy is slack domestic consumer demand. 美国经济面临的一大挑战是国内消费者需求衰退。（2011. 12）② The booming economy means that people are working harder. 经济发展繁荣意味着人们的工作更加努力。
[03:46.12]grave n. 坟墓；去世‖a. 严重的；严峻的；庄严的 示例 ① Many experts now believe that given the right policies, the effects, though grave, need not be catastrophic. 现在，许多专家认为，如果有正确的政策， 虽然影响严重但不会是毁灭性的。（2010. 12） ② He looked very grave when he told us the importance of the event. 他对我们讲述这起事件的重要性时表情非常严肃。
[03:54.87]conservative a. 保守的；谨慎的‖n. 保守者；保守党党员 示例 ① The use of deferential language is symbolic of the Confucian ideal of the woman, which dominates conservative gender norms in Japan. 敬语的使用是儒家理想妇女的标志，它统治着日本保守的性别准则。（2007. 6） ② Nowadays there are only a few conservatives among the young people. 现在的年轻人只有少数是保守的。
[04:02.13]invariably ad. 始终如一地，一贯地 示例 ① A concern for the long term, like uncertainty and fear, is one of the things that nuclear power invariably brings to discussions of future energy. 在关于未来能源的讨论中，诸如不确定性以及恐惧等长远顾虑是核能带来的一贯性问题之一。（The Economist） ② He is waiting for her invariably. 他始终如一地等她。
[04:08.87]moderate a. 适度的；中等的；温和的；合理的‖n. 持温和观点者 v. 缓和；主持 示例 ① A result is that after losing weight, your muscles burn 20 to 25 percent fewer calories during everyday activity and moderate aerobic exercise than those of a person who is naturally at the same weight. 一项发现表明，减肥之后，肌肉在日常活动和轻微有氧运动中消耗的热量比没有减肥的人少20%至25%。（The New York Times）② He is a moderate drinker. 他是一个饮酒有节制的人。
[04:15.59]dimension n. 尺寸；范围；方面 示例 ① First, we decide whether we are superior or inferior to others on certain dimensions, such as attractiveness, intelligence, popularity, etc. 首先，我们得考虑在某些方面我们是优于其他人还是劣于其他人，比如说吸引力、智慧、受欢迎度等。（2012. 12） ② They measured the dimensions of this house. 他们测量了这个房子的面积。
[04:22.56]apart ad. 间隔；分开；除外；成碎片 示例 ① He found that 9-month-old infants could be taught through repeated show-and-tell, to recognise the names of objects that were foreign to them, a result that challenges in some ways the received wisdom that, apart from learning to identify things common to their daily lives, children don't begin to build vocabulary until well into their second year. 他发现可以通过重复的展示和讲述来教会九个月大的婴儿认出那些对他们来说陌生的物体的名字。这一发现在某种程度上挑战了那个已被接受的正确判断，即除了学会识别那些日常生活中的事物，孩子要满两周岁的时候才开始构建词汇。（2006. 12） ② Tom always keeps himself apart from others. 汤姆总是与其他人保持距离。
[04:29.04]logical a. 必然的，合乎情理的；符合逻辑的 示例 ① If a secretary, say, is hired for a job that requires typing ability of at least 80 words a minute and turns out to be capable of only 50 words a minute, she will lose her job in no time. There is a logical standard for this job; performance is easily measured. 假设一位秘书在应聘时被要求每分钟要能够打80个字，但录用之后被发现每分钟只能打50个字，那么她很快就会被炒鱿鱼，因为有一个合乎常理的标准在那里，其表现如何很容易被衡量出来。（The Washington Post）② What he does is a logical thing to do in the circumstances. 他所做的不过是在那种环境下应该做的事。
[04:38.51]racial a. 种族的；人种的 示例 ① Those trying to address issues of racial inequality need to constantly remind people of the inequalities that still exist to counteract the Obama effect, she says. 她说，那些试图解决种族不平等问题的人要时时提醒人们不平等现象仍然存在，以抵消“奥巴马效应”。（2010. 6）② He could not get a job because of racial discrimination. 因为种族歧视，他无法找到工作。
[04:44.17]disgust n. 厌恶，反感‖v. 使厌恶，使反感 示例 ① As a visiting professor at the Harvard Business School in 1989, he ended his work there disgusted with his students' overwhelming lust for money. 他于1989年在哈佛商学院担任客座教授，后来由于厌恶自己的学生对金钱的狂热贪欲而终止了那里的工作。（2006. 12） ② His behaviour really disgusted me. 他的行为着实让我感到恶心。
[04:50.02]interaction n. 相互作用，相互影响，互动 示例 ① The central notion of social learning theories is that people learn attitudes, beliefs, and behaviours through social interaction. 社会学习理论的核心概念即人们通过社会互动来学习他人的态度、信仰及行为方式。（2013. 6） ② The interaction between parents and their children is very important. 父母和孩子之间的互动非常重要。
